{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1781532483,"nonce":"LXOC7GA8uilORN4kM8S2v4XN/YA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGKosaA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/278#issuecomment-4708772968"},"message":"## Apply as a field hotfix on gabby (then import here)\n\nDecision: apply this lake-side as a **field-mode hotfix on gabby** (echoboats origin\nis gitcloud there → field mode: edit main tree, commit to `jazzy`, push to gitcloud,\nno PR), and reconcile to GitHub later via `/import-field-changes` referencing **this\nissue (#278)** instead of opening a fresh import issue. No dev-side PR is being opened\n(it would diverge from the field commit).\n\n### Exact change — `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`\nIn the existing `/**/chart_datum:` block, add one line:\n```yaml\n/**/chart_datum:\n  ros__parameters:\n    map_frame: bizzy/map\n    chart_datum_frame: bizzy/chart_datum\n    base_frame: bizzy/base_link\n    mhhw_frame: bizzy/chart_datum_mhhw\n    lake_datum: 52.3        # WGS84 ellipsoidal lake surface (RTK; no tide). Wins outright.\n```\nDo **not** add `lake_datum_mhhw` (zero tidal range would make sea_surface_estimator\nreject every tide estimate → map_tide stalls — see issue body).\n\n### Field commit (on gabby)\n- Hooks run as normal — **no `--no-verify`**. Use the agent commit identity.\n- Watch for a `no-commit-to-branch` pre-commit hook listing `jazzy` (would block the\n  direct field commit); if present that's a repo-config concern, don't bypass it.\n- `git push` to gitcloud after committing.\n\n### Apply to the running boat\n`lake_datum` is **not live-updatable** — `chart_datum_node` reads it once in\n`on_configure`, no on-set-parameters callback. So `ros2 param set` won't take; the\nnode must be **restarted** (or lifecycle cleanup→configure) to pick up 52.3. Easiest:\nnext core bringup. Verify: node logs `lake_datum override set: chart_datum 52.300 m`\nand the `bizzy/chart_datum` TF appears at 52.3.\n\n### Later (dev side)\n`/import-field-changes` → branch/PR from the gitcloud commit → link **#278**.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1781588151,"nonce":"yMsxcif3TVCcHC736DZMkOxhe7I=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGQ4nwA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/278#issuecomment-4715325376"},"message":"## Refined lake_datum from in-water nav: **≈ 48.88 m** (full-pool), not 52.3\n\nThe wired `lake_datum: 52.3` is **~3.5 m too high** — it was read off the boat **on the trailer** before launch. Derivation below uses the boat's own georeferenced nav z (SBG-free) plus the measured waterline and the lake gauge.\n\n### Derivation\n```\nbase_link in-water z  (/bizzy/odom -\u003e bizzy/base_link, WGS84 ellipsoidal)   48.737 m\n+ waterline offset    (base_link -\u003e water surface, measured #282)            0.030 m\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncurrent water surface (2026-06-15)                                          48.767 m\n+ below-full          (lake-surface gauge 65.5\" vs full 61\" = 4.5\")          0.114 m\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nFULL-POOL lake datum                                                      ≈ 48.88 m\n```\n- **Instantaneous (today's) surface ≈ 48.77 m**; **full-pool ≈ 48.88 m** (stable chart datum — apply the daily below-full offset when reducing a given day's soundings).\n\n### Evidence the 52.3 was the trailer\nFriday (06-12) odom z time series: **52.3–52.4 m while on the trailer** (18:21–18:23, stationary, out of water) → descends as it's lowered → **stabilizes at 48.73 m from 18:31 once afloat**. `52.3 − 48.7 ≈ 3.6 m` = the trailer height.\n\n| | base_link z (in-water) |\n|---|---|\n| Friday 06-12 (post-launch ≥18:31 UTC) | 48.728 m (std 0.045, n=185,608) |\n| Today 06-15 (full in-water day) | 48.737 m (std 0.037, n=291,505) |\n\n**Both in-water days agree to ~1 cm** — the datum is solid; 52.3 was a single bad sample.\n\n### Notes\n- **Source:** `/bizzy/odom` z (the fused nav, ArduPilot FCU-EKF3 per #91 — **not** the SBG). Independent SBG cross-check agrees: gps_pos ellipsoidal = MSL 82.37 + undulation −32.79 = 49.58 m at the antenna; minus the 0.89 m antenna height = 48.69 m base_link, consistent with 48.73.\n- **Caveat:** assumes Friday lake level ≈ today's. The ~1 cm two-day agreement supports this; a Friday gauge reading would confirm.\n\n### Action\n- Update boat config `lake_datum: 52.3 -\u003e 48.88` (full-pool) — one-line, as this issue anticipated.\n- **Dependents carrying the old 52.3 to update:** UMA #148 (Phase-2 imports — \"carries the +52.3\") and the bathy costmap #164.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1781608947,"nonce":"ta1o+7JFEWrkQ+peqYbOJdRPAGk=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABFhpd9M8AAAAGPbfgYQ"},"status":2}]}